  Rows are COLUMNS of one forward, each with its own trajectory, so a repeated
  depth is an independent view of it and not a duplicate.  Under the ring,
  write vector j always lands at rows congruent to j (mod W), so whichever map
  wins stays addressable and the depth-slice ablation survives.

